# ZenTomato — build-time configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is git-ignored and is
# the ONLY place on disk that holds a real credential. `scripts/gen-secrets.sh`
# turns it into the git-ignored `Support/Secrets.xcconfig` that Xcode actually
# reads; nothing reads `.env` at runtime.
#
# THE VALUES BELOW ARE EMPTY ON PURPOSE. This file is committed, so the repo
# documents which keys exist without ever holding one. If you find a value here,
# that is a secret leak — remove it and rotate the credential.
#
# NOTHING HERE HAS TO BE FILLED IN TODAY. Copying this file to `.env` unchanged
# is enough to build the app and run every check. See the note on the Todoist
# keys below for when that changes.
#
#     cp .env.example .env      # then edit .env
#     make secrets              # regenerate Support/Secrets.xcconfig
#
# Continuous integration has no `.env`. The workflow writes one from GitHub
# Actions encrypted secrets before it builds.

# --- Todoist. NOT YET REQUIRED — leave them empty and everything still builds.
#
# Nothing in this repository reads a Todoist credential today. There is no
# Todoist code here at all: that feature (F3) has not been built. So an empty
# value is written straight through as an empty build setting and the app
# compiles, the tests run, and continuous integration goes green without them.
#
# THEY BECOME REQUIRED IN F3, the first piece of work that actually reads one.
# At that point `gen-secrets.sh` stops writing them through empty and starts
# failing by name if one is blank — because from then on an empty client secret
# builds an app that works right up until somebody tries to sign in.
#
# Fill them in whenever you like before then; nothing breaks either way.

# The Todoist OAuth application's client identifier, from the Todoist developer
# console (chore C3). Not a secret in the cryptographic sense, but it belongs
# with its partner rather than hard-coded in a Swift file.
TODOIST_CLIENT_ID=

# The Todoist OAuth application's client secret. A real credential. It is
# accepted that a shipped app cannot hide this; that trade was ratified on the
# understanding that this build is never distributed to anyone else.
TODOIST_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The custom URL scheme Todoist redirects back to after sign-in, WITHOUT the
# "://" — for example `zentomato`. It must match the redirect URI registered in
# the Todoist developer console exactly.
TODOIST_OAUTH_CALLBACK_SCHEME=

# --- Also optional, and permanently so.

# Apple Developer Team ID, used for signing builds installed on a real device.
# Simulator builds are made with code signing switched off entirely, so leaving
# this empty is fine until there is a phone in the loop (chore C4). It lives
# here so that regenerating the Xcode project does not lose the signing team.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=
